A||||14||Fformula88||Jeep Liberty... cute ute?||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||11-28-2001||12:12 PM||||I guess I feel strongly enough about this to post it... Jeep has taken its Wrangler/Jeep image and appears to have turned it into a cute 'ute.  Sure its a good off-roader, and by all accounts a worthy successor to the Cherokee.  But I cannot get past the fact that the front end wrangler-esque styling is more cute ute than tough off-roader.  Am I imagining this or does anyone else see it too?<P>I generally hate SUV's anyway, but I always did think Jeeps were cool.  At least a Wrangler isn't meant to be an overgrown station wagon!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever3000||11-28-2001||12:24 PM||||You're darn right it's a good off-roader, I drove one when Chrysler brought their traveling "Proving Grounds" thing to Houston.  I was shocked by what the Liberty could do!  As for the looks, I don't really have much opinion one way or the other.  It's fine with me, I wouldn't mind having one, but they're nothing special.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||WampusCat||11-28-2001||12:29 PM||||Just remember that it can't corner on pavement like a Fiero, or you might wind up like the AutoWeek test driver: <A HREF="http://www.autoweek.com/cat_content.mv?port_code=autoweek&cat_code=carnews&loc_code=index&content_code=02945750" TARGET=_blank>http://www.autoweek.com/cat_content.mv?port_code=autoweek&cat_code=carnews&loc_code=index&content_code=02945750</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||11-28-2001||12:45 PM||||CUTE?  Personally, I don't care for the front end design at all, it looks like something out of a cartoon because the grill and headlights are so accentuated.  Just my .02 buck.  Oh, and if you're buying something for offroad capabilities, nothin' wrong with a 60/70s CJ-5! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||falconhulk||11-28-2001||03:10 PM||||The liberty is cartoonish!!  Its also out of proportion from the back.  It seems to be to tall for its width.  I dont like it at all.  the interior on the other hand in fantastic.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||11-28-2001||04:52 PM||||Wow..Didn't they go into damage control mode to protect their baby. Plain and simple. It rolled. LOL<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||11-28-2001||04:58 PM||||&lt;rant&gt;I think the liberty is disgusting.  As much as I dislike Jeeps, I think the cherokee was sooo much better.  And off-road capabilities?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> do you think that's going to matter to the yuppy soccer mom that buys it because she wants to be 'trendy'?  &lt;/rant&gt;<P>ok I think I'm done... sorry if I offended anyone  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rex||11-28-2001||05:31 PM||||I simply think the front end is a "jeep thing" to each there own, but I like every thing about the liberty. The price is the most attractive thing in terms of bang for the buck. Look under one, how they are built is impressing,very well put together. I don't own one.......yet!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fformula88||11-28-2001||05:59 PM||||I am glad that I am not alone on the styling!  Cartoonish is a great way to describe it.<P>Off road ability does matter to some people... although the farthest off road 99% of them will get is backing over the flowerbed next to soccer-mom's driveway!  There is still that other 1%!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||11-28-2001||06:11 PM||||Butt-ugly!  Nasty looking girlie car.  If you really want to do some off roading (and have the cash), buy an original Hummer.  NOTHING beats that for off roading.  Period.  (At least not in stock form.)  I drove some of those in the Army.  WOW!  They can do things and go places that are just shy of terrifying.  (Ever tried to drive <I>across</I> a 45* hill?  Bet you can't do that with a Liberty or any other Jeep product for that matter.  You'd be hard pressed to do that in a Fiero.)||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroMontreal||11-28-2001||10:36 PM||||I didn't read all of the replies so I am sorry if I am about to offend people. I think that the New jeep is BUTT UGLY! From the first time that I saw it I thought it looked like crap. I don't know about it's performance, it might be a good little suv, but you would never see me drive something like that unless you gave it to me..Even then.. the only time you'd see me drive it would be when I'm driving in the nearest dealership to trade it in..<BR>Just my 2 cents.. no flames please.<P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif">   <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Master_Sushi||11-29-2001||12:03 AM||||I'd never buy a car/suv/pos that will tip over in a hard corner. <P>A 4X4 pickup with a 350 and some big mudders will give some manly off roadin' also!||||reg||12
Z||000012||artherd||11-29-2001||02:24 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.autoweek.com/images_content/2001_11/liberty_crashed.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.autoweek.com/weekart/2001/1126/liberty_twowheels.jpg"> <P><BR>2,000 words on why I won't be buying one, oh, EVER.<BR>It's no news that the SUV design is inherently flawed, at least in it's implimentation in most consumer craft. (top-heavy) <P>And the front just looks stupid too.<P>Off road?  SUV drivers don't know the difference between All Wheel Drive, and Rodeo Drive.<P>(taken from the porsche fourm)<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000013||Hank is Here||11-29-2001||02:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>CUTE?  Personally, I don't care for the front end design at all, it looks like something out of a cartoon because the grill and headlights are so accentuated.  Just my .02 buck.  Oh, and if you're buying something for offroad capabilities, nothin' wrong with a 60/70s CJ-5!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>CJ-6 is where it is at!  I have a 64 it has a STOCK 72:1 crawl ratio!!!!!  No mods.  Since I have added an overdrive it can carry 65 on the highway and stil idle through most obsticales.   <BR>Just to say here I am not biased I do also own a 66 CJ5 not nearly as fun off road in my opinion, that has the highway advantage. I can carry 75mph in that SAFELY with no wonder or shimmy<P>Hank <P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Nashco||11-29-2001||03:05 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hank is Here:<BR><B> CJ-6 is where it is at!  I have a 64 it has a STOCK 72:1 crawl ratio!!!!!  No mods.  Since I have added an overdrive it can carry 65 on the highway and stil idle through most obsticales.   <BR>Just to say here I am not biased I do also own a 66 CJ5 not nearly as fun off road in my opinion, that has the highway advantage. I can carry 75mph in that SAFELY with no wonder or shimmy<P>Hank <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ha...you must not have too many major mods on the CJ-5  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  My friend's 76 has springs, dropped pitman, body lift, power steering w/steering box brace, 35" radials, and rebuilt everything...thing wonders all over at 70!  That short, narrow wheelbase/tall vehicle thing just makes it tough to drive straight.<P>That thing was a bee-atch to maintain, always needing this or that (given, it was beaten on the trail a lot)...but I swear it could climb up a frickin' tree!  He had the 258 with headers, weber carb, VERY torquey cam from schneider racing, msd, .030 overbore, newer style head, tall gears in the diffs, lockers in front and rear, and stock trans.  We never came across something that it didn't get through.  In the mud bog (about 36" of much) he was the slowest to get through...that thing just kept on chugging, where as most of the v8 and huge tire guys just slammed through it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  The torque of that 258 is amazing!  I couldn't keep up with him in the woods (me in my baja VW)..but in the sand I could go faster everywhere, had to hit the big hills at about 25 to make it to the top  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Ok, sorry for interrupting the thread, just me and my silly *good* memories.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>*forgot an important mod <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">*<P><p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
